  "question": {
    "text": "The focal length of a thin biconvex lens is $20 \\mathrm{~cm}$. When an object is moved from a distance of $25 \\mathrm{~cm}$ in front of it to $50 \\mathrm{~cm}$, the magnification of its image changes from $m_{25}$ to $m_{50}$. The ratio $\\frac{m_{25}}{m_{50}}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{1}{v}-\\frac{1}{u}=\\frac{1}{f}$ or\n$$\n\\frac{u}{v}-1=\\frac{u}{f}\n$$\n$\\begin{array}{rlrl} & \\text { or } & \\frac{u}{v} & =\\left(\\frac{u+f}{f}\\right) \\\\ \\therefore & m=\\frac{v}{u} & =\\left(\\frac{f}{u+f}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{m_{25}}{m_{50}} & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{20}{-25+20}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{20}{-50+20}\\right)}=6\\end{array}$\n$\\therefore$ answer is 6 .",
    "image": null
  },
